<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stracimir Balšić</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1373</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stracimir Balšić was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balsa-i">Balša I</a> and, with his brothers Đurađ I and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balsa-ii">Balša II</a>, one of the lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a>. He held lands in the south of Zeta and died in 1373. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durad-ii-balsic">Đurađ II Balšić</a> later ruled the whole family domain from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Skadar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stracimir-balsic.jpg" alt="Stracimir Balšić" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gmihail at Serbian Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 rs · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grave_inscription_of_Stracimir_Balsic.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
